  This directory contains your public html files and folders. All
files you wish to make available for to the world wide web should be
world readable. All subdirectories must also be world executable.
Please be aware that files and directories which you place here will
be read and possibly cached by internet search engines; exercise
appropriate caution when publishing information here.


## Local preview and templates

This site now uses GitHub Pages-compatible Jekyll templates to avoid duplicated page chrome:

- `_layouts/default.html` contains the shared HTML `<head>`, top navigation include, and footer include.
- `_includes/header.html` centralizes navigation links used across pages.
- `_includes/footer.html` contains the shared footer.
- Content pages use Jekyll front matter (for example, `layout: default`) and keep only page-specific body content.

To preview locally:

1. Install Jekyll/Bundler (if not already available): `gem install bundler jekyll`
2. From the repository root, run: `bundle exec jekyll serve`
3. Open the local URL shown in the terminal (usually `http://127.0.0.1:4000`).
